# The far pans (rooms/far_pans.adv). Optional, no puzzle: Ansel on his barrel, and the things the
# reunion had no room for. His mother, the stars, the three years, and an apology that arrives in
# the wrong order, as his always do. The goodbye walks them back up to the camp together.
dialogue pans
  node root ansel "Best seat on Gullet Key. You can see the old girl's masts from here. None of her holes. I've been keeping it for somebody."
    > "Tell me about my mother. I have four things." if not seen:pans.lise -> lise
    > "You named the stars wrong on purpose. I'd correct you." if not seen:pans.stars -> stars
    > "I kept the outbound book for three years." if not seen:pans.book -> book
    > "Quill's watching us from the camp." if not seen:pans.watching -> watching
    > "I'd better run that flag up." -> go
  # Down at the pans again.
  node again ansel "Back again? Good. The barrel's been asking after you."
    > "Tell me about my mother. I have four things." if not seen:pans.lise -> lise
    > "You named the stars wrong on purpose. I'd correct you." if not seen:pans.stars -> stars
    > "I kept the outbound book for three years." if not seen:pans.book -> book
    > "Quill's watching us from the camp." if not seen:pans.watching -> watching
    > "I'd better run that flag up." -> go
  # Between subjects.
  node more narrator "The fog lifts a little further off the lagoon."
    > "Tell me about my mother. I have four things." if not seen:pans.lise -> lise
    > "You named the stars wrong on purpose. I'd correct you." if not seen:pans.stars -> stars
    > "I kept the outbound book for three years." if not seen:pans.book -> book
    > "Quill's watching us from the camp." if not seen:pans.watching -> watching
    > "I'd better run that flag up." -> go

  # Lise: the L on every flag (ansel.adv, log.adv).
  node lise ansel "Four's a good number. Go on. I'll tell you which ones are true."
    -> four
  node four fenn "Thread. Canvas. Her thimble on the hall table. And she sang the wrong words to everything."
    -> three
  node three ansel "Three out of four. She sang the right words to the wrong tunes, to annoy me. She was right about everything else. That was worse."
    > "I don't remember her face." -> face
    > "Sing me one. The way she did." -> sing
  node face ansel "It's on my cabin wall, a bit crooked. You wear it, you know. Just before you're right about something. I've missed it every day."
    -> more
  node sing narrator "He sings two lines of a shanty to the tune of a hymn, quite badly. In the next pan, the heron turns its back on us."
    -> better
  node better ansel "She did it better. She did everything better. And she never let me forget it. I'd like to be reminded."
    -> more

  # The night watch: "He used to name the stars wrong on purpose, so I'd correct him." (watch.adv)
  node stars ansel "On purpose?"
    -> sky
  node sky narrator "He looks up at a sky with no stars in it. As if one might turn up and vouch for him."
    -> nope
  node nope ansel "Son, I have never known which one's the Hook. Rook did the stars. Your mother did the stars. I did the shouting."
    -> took
  node took ansel "She corrected me every clear night. When she was gone, you took over. You were six, and very firm about it."
    note named_stars "My father never knew one star from another. My mother corrected him every clear night. When she died I took over. I was six."
    > "I thought it was a game." -> game
    > "You could have just learned them." -> learn
    > "Quill says someone should correct you." if seen:watch.corrected -> told
  node game ansel "It was. It was the last one she was here for."
    -> hook
  node learn ansel "And lose the only navigator I had who couldn't see over the chart table? Not likely."
    -> hook
  node told ansel "Did she! Then I'll need the pair of you. I'm wrong about a great many stars."
    -> hook
  node hook ansel "…Don't tell anyone I said any of this. I've a reputation as a navigator to keep up."
    -> more

  # The three years, and the compass on the hall table (items.adv).
  node book ansel "Did you! Every ship out of Vela, in your own hand?"
    -> tally
  node tally fenn "Every one. I stamped them hard, so they'd come back. They all did but yours. Five of them came back empty."
    -> here
  node here ansel "…They're here, son. All six crews, raking salt. You've been stamping them home for three years and didn't know it."
    > "Two of them still owe harbour dues." -> dues
    > "I dusted round your compass. On the hall table." -> dust
  node dues ansel "Ha! Then we'd better get them home to pay. I'll break it gently. They've had a hard three years."
    -> more
  node dust ansel "Oh, son. I'm sorry."
    -> dust2
  node dust2 ansel "…About the dusting. It's a terrible table for dust. Your mother said so the day we bought it."
    -> dust3
  node dust3 ansel "And the rest of it. Sorry about the rest of it. I'll get the order right one of these days."
    -> more

  node watching ansel "I know. She's been at it since the store hut, pretending not to, very badly. What does she call you?"
    > "Cargo." -> cargo
    > "Cargo. Mostly." if aff >= 12 -> mostly
  node mostly ansel "Mostly! Oh, son. Mostly is how it starts. Your mother called me “the hazard” for two years. Then one day she didn't."
    -> more
  node cargo ansel "Cargo! Oh, that's lovely. Cargo's the whole point of a ship, son. Everything else is just there to carry it."
    -> more

  node go ansel "Go on, then. Your mother hated a flag left in a pocket."
    -> wrong
  node wrong narrator "We walk back up to the camp together. He goes wrong twice on the way, on perfectly flat salt."
    go salt_camp sound none
